# Triage — project layout

## Spring Boot application

- Entry point: `src/main/java/com/qligent/triage/TriageApplication.java`
- REST controllers: `src/main/java/com/qligent/triage/controller/`
- Config: `src/main/resources/application.yaml`
- Build: Gradle (`build.gradle`, `gradlew`)

## Zephyr Scale API (reference only, not runtime code)

Example HTTP calls and captured responses for [Zephyr Scale](https://smartbear.com/test-management/zephyr-scale/) live outside `src/`:

| Purpose | Path |
|--------|------|
| Example requests (curl, etc.) | `Zephyr Scale API/requests/` |
| Example API responses (JSON) | `Zephyr Scale API/responses/` |

Pair files by name prefix when possible (e.g. `Get test cases B2C - code` ↔ `Get test cases B2C - response`).

When implementing Zephyr integration, read matching pairs from these folders before inventing request/response shapes.

**Secrets:** API tokens must not be committed. Do not read or echo `Zephyr Scale API Access Token.txt` in chat output.
